{
  "title": "84: al-Insheqaaq الإنشقاق",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nاِذَا السَّمَآءُ انْشَقَّتْۙ‏(1)\nEZAS SAMAAA-UN SHAQQAT.\nWhen the sky is split open\nوَاَذِنَتْ لِرَبِّهَا وَحُقَّتْۙ‏(2)\nWA AZENAT LE-RABBEHAA WA HUQQAT.\nand gives ear to its Lord as it should.\nوَاِذَا الْاَرْضُ مُدَّتْؕ‏(3)\nWA EZAL ARZO MUDDAT.\nWhen the earth is spread out\nوَاَلْقَتْ مَا فِيْهَا وَتَخَلَّتْۙ‏(4)\nWA ALQAT MAA FEEHAA WA TAKHALLAT.\nand throws out what is in it, emptying itself,\nوَاَذِنَتْ لِرَبِّهَا وَحُقَّتْؕ‏(5)\nWA AZENAT LE-RABBEHA WA HUQQAT.\nand gives ear to its Lord as it should.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الْاِنْسَانُ اِنَّكَ كَادِحٌ اِلٰى رَبِّكَ كَدْحًا فَمُلٰقِيْهِ‌ۚ‏(6)\nYAA-AYYOHAL INSAANO INNAKA KAADEHUN ELAA RABBEKA KADHAN FA-MOLAAQEEH.\nO man! You are labouring toward your Lord laboriously, and you will encounter Him.\nفَاَمَّا مَنْ اُوْتِىَ كِتٰبَهٗ بِيَمِيْنِهٖۙ‏(7)\nFA-AMMAA MAN OOTEYA KETAABAHU BE-YAMEENEHI.\nThen, as for him who is given his record [of deeds] in his right hand,\nفَسَوْفَ يُحَاسَبُ حِسَابًا يَّسِيْرًا ۙ‏(8)\nFA-SAWFA YOHAASABO HESAABANY YASEERANW.\nhe will receive an easy reckoning,\nوَّيَنْقَلِبُ اِلٰٓى اَهْلِهٖ مَسْرُوْرًا ؕ‏(9)\nWA YANQALEBO ELAA AHLEHI MASROORAA.\nand he will return to his folks joyfully.\nوَاَمَّا مَنْ اُوْتِىَ كِتٰبَهٗ وَرَآءَ ظَهْرِهٖۙ‏(10)\nWA AMMAA MAN OOTEYA KETAABAHU WARAAA-A ZAHREHI.\nBut as for him who is given his record from behind his back,\nفَسَوْفَ يَدْعُوْا ثُبُوْرًا ۙ‏(11)\nFA-SAWFA YAD-O’O SOBOORANW.\nhe will pray for annihilation\nوَّيَصْلٰى سَعِيْرًا ؕ‏(12)\nWA YASLAA SA-E’ERAA.\nand enter the Blaze.\nاِنَّهٗ كَانَ فِىْۤ اَهْلِهٖ مَسْرُوْرًا ؕ‏(13)\nINNAHU KAANA FEE AHLEHI MASROORAA.\nIndeed he used to be joyful among his folk,\nاِنَّهٗ ظَنَّ اَنْ لَّنْ يَّحُوْرَ ۛۚ‏(14)\nINNAHU ZANNA AL LAN-Y YAHOOR.\nand he thought that he would never return.\nبَلٰٓى ۛۚ اِنَّ رَبَّهٗ كَانَ بِهٖ بَصِيْرًا ؕ‏(15)\nBALAA, INNA RABBAHU KAANA BEHI BASEERAA.\nYes, his Lord had been watching him.\nفَلَاۤ اُقْسِمُ بِالشَّفَقِۙ‏(16)\nFALAA UQSEMO BISH-SHAFAQE.\nI swear by the evening glow,\nوَالَّيْلِ وَمَا وَسَقَۙ‏(17)\nWAL LAYLE WA MAA WASAQA.\nby the night and what it is fraught with,\nوَالْقَمَرِ اِذَا اتَّسَقَۙ‏(18)\nWAL QAMARE EZAT TASAQA.\nby the moon when it blooms full:\nلَتَرْكَبُنَّ طَبَقًا عَنْ طَبَقٍؕ‏(19)\nLA-TARKABUNNA TABAQN A’N TABAQ.\nyou will surely fare from stage to stage.\nفَمَا لَهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَۙ‏(20)\nFAMAA LAHUM LAA YOAMENOONA.\nWhat is the matter with them that they will not believe,\nوَاِذَا قُرِئَ عَلَيْهِمُ الْقُرْاٰنُ لَا يَسْجُدُوْنَ ؕ ۩‏(21)\nWA EZAA QORE-A A’LAYHEMUL QUR-AANO LAA YASJODOONA.\nand will not prostrate when the Quran is recited to them?\nبَلِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا يُكَذِّبُوْنَۖ‏(22)\nBALIL LAZEENA KAFAROO YOKAZZEBOON.\nIndeed, the faithless impugn [the Apostle],\nوَاللّٰهُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا يُوْعُوْنَۖ‏(23)\nWAL-LAAHO A-A’LAMO BEMAA YOO-O’ON.\nand Allah knows best what they keep to themselves.\nفَبَشِّرْهُمْ بِعَذَابٍ اَلِيْمٍۙ‏(24)\nFA-BASH-SHIRHUM BE-A’ZAABIN ALEEMIN.\nSo inform them of a painful punishment,\nاِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ لَهُمْ اَجْرٌ غَيْرُ مَمْنُوْنٍ‏(25)\nILLAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE LAHUM AJRUN GHAYRO MAMNOON.\nexcepting such as are faithful and do righteous deeds: for them there will be an everlasting reward.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Insheqaaq (The Bursting Asunder)\nThis Surah has 25 verses and it was revealed in Makkah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that the one who recites this Surah will not get his book of deeds from his back on the Day of Reckoning.\nIf written and worn by a pregnant woman, the delivery of the baby becomes easy. However, it is important that after delivery, this Surah should be kept away from her. If this Surah is tied on any animal (eg. camels or horses) then it keeps them safe."
